cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Velri: Native C23 and Khronos Slang AOT Neural-Network Inference Engine"
message: "If you use Velri in software, benchmarks, or research, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "Vemloir"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/velri-inference/velri"
url: "https://velri-inference.github.io"
abstract: >-
  Velri is a native neural-network and LLM inference engine written in C23 and C++23
  behind a public C23 API, using Khronos Slang (slangc) ahead-of-time compilation for
  unified CPU (x86-64 AVX2/AVX-512 VNNI, ARM64, RISC-V 64) and Vulkan 1.3 / SPIR-V 1.6
  compute kernels with zero runtime Python, PyTorch, CUDA, or compiler dependencies.
keywords:
  - llm-inference
  - inference-engine
  - c23
  - khronos-slang
  - vulkan
  - spir-v
  - avx512
  - vnni
  - offloading
  - quantization
  - vtq
  - neural-networks
